{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1673","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1673","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1673\",\"parent_revision\":\"774f565ca4d7380708871708989e7443d2fa7c7f3b2a0b4e38bdf4f4ac173bf5\",\"root_revision\":\"774f565ca4d7380708871708989e7443d2fa7c7f3b2a0b4e38bdf4f4ac173bf5\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nDocumentation throughout the plugin embeds derived counts inline (\\\"8 required sections\\\", \\\"Skills Overview (30)\\\", \\\"5 agents\\\") instead of referencing the source of truth. These counts drift silently when the source changes.\\n\\n**Observed in #996:** adding one agent and one required section required updating 17 instances of hardcoded counts across 11 files.\\n\\n**Active drift confirmed today:** `CLAUDE.md` Skills Overview heading says \\\"(30)\\\" but there are 40 `SKILL.md` files in `skills/`. The \\\"7 sections\\\" references in `state-machine.md` and `item.md` conflict with the actual 8-entry validation table in `finalize.md` \u2014 evidence of a past undiscovered drift event.\\n\\n**Scope (fully enumerated):** 27 specific instances across 8 operational files.\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type**: recurring-pattern \u2014 documentation drift via embedded derived counts  \\n**Pattern**: count embedded at authoring time, no lint enforcement, no single reference token\\n</div>\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Must change (8 operational files):**\\n\\n1. `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/finalize.md`\\n2. `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/start.md`\\n3. `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-backlog-item/references/groomer-output-validation.md`\\n4. `plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/references/item-schema.md`\\n5. `plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/references/state-machine.md`\\n6. `plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/templates/item.md`\\n7. `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-lifecycle.md`\\n8. `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md`\\n\\n**Source of truth (read-only reference):**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/finalize.md` lines 99\u2013107 \u2014 required sections validation table\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **27 hardcoded count instances across 8 operational files**\\n- `CLAUDE.md` Skills Overview actively wrong: heading says 30, actual is 40\\n- 7-vs-8 section count split across docs \u2014 conflicting contracts\\n- Every future addition to required-sections table or agents/skills directories requires manual updates to all 27 instances with no mechanism to detect missed updates\\n</div>\\n\\n## Priority\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**P1** \u2014 maintenance burden confirmed: #996 required 17 manual updates across 11 files for a one-unit change. `CLAUDE.md` Skills Overview count is wrong **today** (30 heading, 40 actual). The 7-vs-8 section count split means some documentation describes a different grooming contract than the one enforced by `finalize.md`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Benefits\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Section count references stay correct when finalize.md table changes\\n- Agent/skill count references stay correct when directories change\\n- 7-vs-8 split resolved by pointing all references to single table\\n- Future contributors cannot introduce silent drift \u2014 reference pattern makes source explicit\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Zero instances of hardcoded section counts (7, 8, or any number) adjacent to the grooming sections concept in operational files under `plugins/development-harness/` (excluding `*.draft.md`)\\n- [ ] Zero instances of hardcoded agent/skill counts in `CLAUDE.md` overview headings \u2014 use \\\"Skills Overview\\\" / \\\"Agents Overview\\\" without inline counts, OR cite the source directory without embedding a number\\n- [ ] `docs/backlog-lifecycle.md:253` \\\"7 sections\\\" inconsistency resolved to match finalize.md table (8)\\n- [ ] `state-machine.md` and `item.md` \\\"7 canonical sections\\\" updated to reference finalize.md table rather than embedding a number\\n- [ ] All replacements reference source: `skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/finalize.md` lines 99\u2013107\\n- [ ] No new hardcoded counts introduced during the fix\\n- [ ] `uv run prek run --files <file>` passes after each file edit\\n</div>\\n\\n## Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**S (Small)** \u2014 Pure text search-and-replace across 8 files, no logic change. Uniform replacement pattern. ~1\u20132 hours for sequential edits with lint validation per file.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want **hardcoded counts removed from documentation and replaced with references to the source of truth** so that **counts stay correct automatically when source lists change**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Documentation smell identified during #996 implementation \u2014 derived data duplication pattern\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-08\\n- **Groomed**: 2026-04-09\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:f9e088228ab3ee7bfddbc2e2a3bf0caf -->\\n</div>\\n\\n## Root Cause Analysis 6 Sigma\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Root cause 1:** No single reference token for \\\"required sections count.\\\" The list lives in `finalize.md` validation table (lines 99\u2013107) but there is no established convention for deferring to it \u2014 authors write counts inline because it is faster.\\n\\n**Root cause 2:** No linting rule detects hardcoded numeric counts adjacent to structural terms. `.pre-commit-config.yaml` runs `markdownlint-cli2`, `skilllint`, and `ruff` \u2014 none detect `\\\"N sections\\\"` patterns. Count drift produces no CI failure.\\n\\n**Root cause 3:** Counts embedded during initial authoring propagated silently. Writing \\\"all 8 sections\\\" vs \\\"all required sections (defined in finalize.md)\\\" is a micro-decision with no immediate feedback; the wrong choice is undetectable until a human notices.\\n\\n**Secondary inconsistency exposed:** `state-machine.md`, `item.md`, and `backlog-lifecycle.md:253` say \\\"7 sections\\\" while `finalize.md` validation table lists 8. The 7-vs-8 split is itself a symptom \u2014 a section was added to the table without updating all referencing files.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Scope Enumerated Files And Instances\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n| File | Lines | Instances | Note |\\n|------|-------|-----------|------|\\n| `skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/finalize.md` | 96, 120, 148 | 3 | Source of truth \u2014 count is redundant here too |\\n| `skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/start.md` | 64 | 1 | Derived from finalize.md table |\\n| `skills/groom-backlog-item/references/groomer-output-validation.md` | 12, 65, 66 | 3 | Includes Mermaid node label (use `<br>` not link) |\\n| `skills/backlog/references/item-schema.md` | 23, 42, 157, 163, 173 | 5 | Mixed 7/8 \u2014 both wrong to embed |\\n| `skills/backlog/references/state-machine.md` | 48, 63, 64, 196 | 4 | Stale \\\"7\\\" \u2014 finalize.md table has 8 |\\n| `skills/backlog/templates/item.md` | 11 | 1 | Stale \\\"7\\\" |\\n| `docs/backlog-lifecycle.md` | 64, 84, 114, 144, 253, 286, 385, 386 | 8 | One stale \\\"7\\\" at line 253 |\\n| `CLAUDE.md` | 224, 230, 237, 247, 270, 285 | 6 | Skills count wrong (30 heading, 40 actual); subcategory counts all derived |\\n| **Total** | | **31** | |\\n\\nDraft (lower priority, not operational):\\n- `docs/backlog-lifecycle.draft.md` \u2014 5 instances\\n</div>\\n\\n## Implementation Notes\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Replacement pattern for section counts:**\\n\\n```text\\nBEFORE: \\\"Check all 8 required sections are present\\\"\\nAFTER:  \\\"Check all required sections are present (defined in finalize.md validation table)\\\"\\n\\nBEFORE: \\\"set by groom-backlog-item when all 8 sections present\\\"  \\nAFTER:  \\\"set by groom-backlog-item when all required sections present (see finalize.md)\\\"\\n```\\n\\n**CLAUDE.md overview headings:**\\n\\n```text\\nBEFORE: \\\"## Skills Overview (30)\\\"\\nAFTER:  \\\"## Skills Overview\\\"\\n\\nBEFORE: \\\"## Agents Overview (21)\\\"\\nAFTER:  \\\"## Agents Overview\\\"\\n```\\n\\nSubcategory counts like `**SAM workflow (4):**` should also be removed \u2014 they derive from the list immediately following and will drift.\\n\\n**Mermaid node labels** (`finalize.md:120`, `groomer-output-validation.md:65`): Cannot use markdown links inside Mermaid node labels. Replace count with prose inside the label: `\\\"Check all required sections\\\\nper finalize.md table\\\"`.\\n\\n**State-machine 7-vs-8 resolution:** `state-machine.md` was authored when count was 7. The operational source of truth is `finalize.md` validation table. Update to reference the table. Also audit the \\\"Step 9\\\" reference (line 63) \u2014 it may refer to an old step number that no longer applies.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"3413b22de465b7610d7c0a5977047b72b8606330c133900fa77d387f3aa48ec6\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVV-E0A\"}"}